{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination","id":852981,"title":"NPC Question: (BSD?) Abomination","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-25T08:27:49-07:00","id":852981,"title":"NPC Question: (BSD?) Abomination","content":"I know ALL the reasons not to allow such a beast in a game. WW and various purists can be quoted all over the place.<br /> I'm not here for that.<br /> I'm here to get some help and input into making such a Beast viable as an NPC who will start as an Ally, become a Mentor, and eventually be revealed as a terrible Enemy. All over centuries.<br /> So, I need suggestions on making a character that CAN last the centuries.<br /> Not a Harano-crushed soul who greets the sun.<br /> Not a raving psycho who commits suicide by Wyrm/Vampire/Garou Pack/etc.<br /> Perhaps he'll go through these stages...I can't really say at this point. <br /> But, let's talk about things like Tribe, Clan, Auspice, Original Cultural Background, etc.<br /> How can we make it work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9106-jimflory","name":"jimflory","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:39:21-07:00","id":853027,"title":"","content":"Why does the NPC have to be a BSD Abomination? I think the same purpose could happen and perhaps be even more dramatic if the NPC was a kinfolk. Or using the established villains and assorted others a Mage might work or even a limited form of Mummy.<br /> I used a Mummy bound to a Wyrm spirit as a master villain in my last chronicle the players had a great deal of difficulty tracking him down and discovering how to permanently end him. <br /> <br /> But going with the Abomination theme.<br /> I would limit the Rank to 3 and pick Children of Gaia as the tribe. I would also tend towards either Lasombra or Ventrue as the Clan. As the OP stated centuries is this going to be a multi-pack chronicle over years?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T10:01:14-07:00","id":853037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jimflory</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination#post852981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can we make it work?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say do so by playing on an abominations strong suit, its potential for power. You should explore idea's as to what an abomination can do that werewolves and vampires can't or won't do individually.<br /> <br /> What happens when you combine gifts with blood magic? How powerful would such abilities be?<br /> <br /> What happens when an Abomination diablerizes a vampire? Would it really loose anything considering it was never human to begin with and killing was second nature to it in life?<br /> <br /> How would such a creature feel knowing it has lost the blessing of gaia? Would it feel abandoned? Would it blame gaia as it was the failure of gaia's own blessings that led to its current state?<br /> <br /> What would happen when a vampires beast was merged with a werewolf's innate rage?<br /> <br /> Here are some things you can add to abominations to make them more vaible as NPC's without changing the current rules.<br /> <br /> Make feeding on supernaturals temporarily suspend an abom's harano and diablerie(aka eating people's souls) return 1 lost permanent gnosis dot.<br /> <br /> Give the abom unique gifts and rites based on its dual nature. Example:<br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Blood Gifts:<br /> <br /> Thanks to an Abominations unique background they are able to blend the the rituals and ritae of blood magic with the rites of the garou. this allows them to study and create unique gifts using the unholy blood.<br /> <br /> Rule's:<br /> <br /> An abomination must have a level in thaumaturgy equal or greater than the rank of the gift they wish to learn/create. Creating a gift hold the same rules as creating a thaum ritual.<br /> <br /> Examples:<br /> <br /> Blood frenzy: rank 3 EXP 10<br /> <br /> An abomination knows the tainted power of blood and the force of the beast within, this gift allows one to focus the rage of the beast into spiritual rage to power their gifts.<br /> <br /> An abomination may spend one BP to gain one rage and vise versa. An abomination may not transfer more blood or rage per turn greater than half their dots of rage.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Spiritual</span></span> vampire: Rank 5 EXP 15<br /> <br /> An abominations vampiric nature bleeds into it's more spiritual aspects, gaining them new powers all their own. Their claws and fangs cry out with their unnatural hunger, draining their foes of strength.<br /> <br /> Whenever an abomination deals damage with it's claw or bite attacks they drain one &quot;energy point&quot; from their targets highest pool(gnosis and rage from garou, blood for vampires, quintessence for mages). What energy is drained goes to the abominations corresponding pool, if the abomination doesn't have one(quintessence) then it's absorbed into blood. If the abominations pools are full then they energy is transferred to healing 1 point heals 1 level of lethal or bashing damage, 3 points to heal aggravated damage. any excess energy remaining by the end of the turn dissipates.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T10:05:10-07:00","id":853040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jimflory</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination#post852981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm here to get some help and input into making such a Beast viable as an NPC who will start as an Ally, become a Mentor, and eventually be revealed as a terrible Enemy. All over centuries.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a, essentially, at odds with the idea of Abominations. It's not that we can't help you come up with an Abomination that will have a reason to chug along for centuries, but without a massive conceptual change to the Abominations they're going to be shitty at both achieving a level of balance to sustain themselves and being the kind of manipulative bastard to be playing the PCs all along.<br /> <br /> The question towards making this viable does start with, &quot;why is this an Abomination?&quot; because that's going to matter a lot to if viability is really possible in the material as written, or if there's going to be a need to make up a lot of house ruled stuff for the NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T10:45:45-07:00","id":853058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination?p=853027#post853027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does the NPC have to be a BSD Abomination?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination?p=853040#post853040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question towards making this viable does start with, &quot;why is this an Abomination?&quot; because that's going to matter a lot to if viability is really possible in the material as written, or if there's going to be a need to make up a lot of house ruled stuff for the NPC.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't. But, the purpose of this particular thread is to explore that possibility. To see if it CAN be done well. If it can, in a way that fits my group and campaign, then I'll be left with the difficulty of deciding if it SHOULD be done. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination?p=853027#post853027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But going with the Abomination theme.<br /> I would limit the Rank to 3 and pick Children of Gaia as the tribe. I would also tend towards either Lasombra or Ventrue as the Clan. As the OP stated centuries is this going to be a multi-pack chronicle over years?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is for a Vampire game so, in truth, it may end up being a single Vampire coterie over many decades or centuries. <br /> Garou will be treated as the Enemy in this Chronicle, though it's entirely possible that the Players (if not the Characters) may see the irony and the truth of things; which is that there will be Good, Evil, and Blame to go around on all sides of this mess.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination?p=853040#post853040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a, essentially, at odds with the idea of Abominations. It's not that we can't help you come up with an Abomination that will have a reason to chug along for centuries, but without a massive conceptual change to the Abominations they're going to be shitty at both achieving a level of balance to sustain themselves and being the kind of manipulative bastard to be playing the PCs all along.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand. What, specifically, do you see as the concepts inherent to the Abomination that would need to be changed for this to be viable? Also, to clarify, this creature doesn't necessarily have to be playing the PCs all along. As this is a Vampire game (they start in the Dark Ages, though this creature's introduction need not be so early), he could grow and change over a long period of time. Each encounter with him could see definite shifts in power, perspective, and goals. He could be honest in his attempts to contribute in early nights, but evolve into something far more sinister by the present time.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9106-jimflory","name":"jimflory","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T11:30:31-07:00","id":853080,"title":"","content":"Well think of clan... a lot of abominations, belong to overl like group... like the only canon abomination ive seen is a silver fang, and a ventrue...<br /> <br /> he doesnt need to be baali or setite, he could be a toreador or triemere...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T13:56:11-07:00","id":853153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jimflory</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination?p=853058#post853058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand. What, specifically, do you see as the concepts inherent to the Abomination that would need to be changed for this to be viable? Also, to clarify, this creature doesn't necessarily have to be playing the PCs all along. As this is a Vampire game (they start in the Dark Ages, though this creature's introduction need not be so early), he could grow and change over a long period of time. Each encounter with him could see definite shifts in power, perspective, and goals. He could be honest in his attempts to contribute in early nights, but evolve into something far more sinister by the present time.</div> </div> </div> </div>The biggest issue is the difficult path of an Abomination managing to find a way to balance Humanity and Ego. Lots of traits linked to these can't be regained if lost. And they're easily lost.<br /> <br /> The easiest life for an Abomination to avoid losing itself is to avoid high levels of stress... which means not getting involved with vampire politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T14:37:15-07:00","id":853168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination?p=853153#post853153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The biggest issue is the difficult path of an Abomination managing to find a way to balance Humanity and Ego. Lots of traits linked to these can't be regained if lost. And they're easily lost.<br /> <br /> The easiest life for an Abomination to avoid losing itself is to avoid high levels of stress... which means not getting involved with vampire politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would, of course, be a poor excuse for a villain <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Then again, it might make for a very amusing variant of the Big Lebowski...<br /> <br /> So, how do Humanity and Ego figure in, exactly? Humanity helps defend against the Beast, and Ego avoids the clutches of the Wyrm? Or is that incorrect?<br /> What role would a vampiric Path play? Could our Wyrm-ridden vamp-wolf find solace in a different Path?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9106-jimflory","name":"jimflory","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T15:57:16-07:00","id":853208,"title":"","content":"in my chronicle i have 1 abomination bsd allied to a baal apostate coterie. The baali are infiltred inside the Cam society, 1 are a powerfull Ventrue apostate, the mission for the baali and bsd is to corrupt/weak the entire city and after that diablerize the &quot;Ante&quot; ( it's only a powerfull mathusa ) who sleep under the city... why? it's only matter of power...<br /> <br /> for the bsd i don't use the classic rules of ego...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6052-rettile-blitch","user":"Rettile&amp;Blitch","date":". 03-25-2016, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6052-rettile-blitch","name":"Rettile&Blitch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T21:40:59-07:00","id":853327,"title":"","content":"Ok this is a Vampire chronicle. That means certain rules can be discarded as needed. First Garou are not human and never have been Garou morality is tied to Garou beliefs which is why in RAW they develop Harano, fall to the Wyrm, walk into sunlight, etc. Now we can discard all Garou spirituality, and develop a sole Vampiric Lupine. Use whatever gifts from any tribe you like, and treat the NPC as a bloodline. Replace all Garou mechanics with Vampire mechanics replacing Gnosis and Rage with blood point expenditures. I would pick a tribe and use the gifts to create the bloodline discipline. Disciplines and Gifts are not equal so this may take a bit of work. The Abomination already has the equivalent of Protean at a high level. <br /> The Wolf Lord bloodline is at best a rumor and at worst a bogey man used to keep younger Vampires in line. Unfortunately it is neither. The Wolf Lords are the result of the Tremere experimenting on Lupines that went tragically wrong for the Tremere. The Wolf Lords developed their signature discipline in a brief time and vanished into the nights. <br /> Bloodline weakness: Silver does aggravated damage and even the touch of silver does lethal damage. Silver can only be soaked with Fortitude.<br /> Disciplines: Celerirty, Fortitude, and the signature discipline based solely on the tribe chosen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T21:52:00-07:00","id":853329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jimflory</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination?p=853168#post853168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which would, of course, be a poor excuse for a villain</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for a manipulative villain. An Abomination that found a good balance by the RAW would be extremely invested in maintaining its little corner of the world as-is, and removing any threats as quickly as possible.<br /> <br /> That's sort of the problem. They're a great character that can move between helpful and antagonist depending on how the PCs goals and its goals align, but the Abomination is generally going to be reacting to threats to its domain that it has probably put a lot into proactively setting up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, how do Humanity and Ego figure in, exactly? Humanity helps defend against the Beast, and Ego avoids the clutches of the Wyrm? Or is that incorrect?<br /> What role would a vampiric Path play? Could our Wyrm-ridden vamp-wolf find solace in a different Path? </div> </div> </div>That's the basics of it. Abominations RAW (though NPC... so again, this is something to consider changing) can't spend XP on Humanity/Paths, or Virtues. So every dot lost is gone for good. And low Humanity means more frenzy triggers, which can reduce Ego since they still use Rage for Frenzy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T03:29:28-07:00","id":853417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination?p=853329#post853329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So every dot lost is gone for good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to recall something, somewhere about an Abomination giving in and serving the Wyrm having its Gnosis replaced. I wish I could remember...<br /> But, anyway, whether BSD or simply a 'Fallen' Garou, what sort of changes or problems would arise from our little monster changing spiritual allegiances?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9106-jimflory","name":"jimflory","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T03:34:24-07:00","id":853418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination?p=853327#post853327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok this is a Vampire chronicle. That means certain rules can be discarded as needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very good point, and one I hadn't considered. I'm used to the idea of using the different 'race' books as needed, but that's really not necessary. I'll have to give that one some thought. Thanks!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9106-jimflory","name":"jimflory","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T07:01:37-07:00","id":853445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination?p=853327#post853327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok this is a Vampire chronicle. That means certain rules can be discarded as needed. First Garou are not human and never have been Garou morality is tied to Garou beliefs which is why in RAW they develop Harano, fall to the Wyrm, walk into sunlight, etc. Now we can discard all Garou spirituality, and develop a sole Vampiric Lupine. Use whatever gifts from any tribe you like, and treat the NPC as a bloodline. Replace all Garou mechanics with Vampire mechanics replacing Gnosis and Rage with blood point expenditures. I would pick a tribe and use the gifts to create the bloodline discipline. Disciplines and Gifts are not equal so this may take a bit of work. The Abomination already has the equivalent of Protean at a high level.<br /> The Wolf Lord bloodline is at best a rumor and at worst a bogey man used to keep younger Vampires in line. Unfortunately it is neither. The Wolf Lords are the result of the Tremere experimenting on Lupines that went tragically wrong for the Tremere. The Wolf Lords developed their signature discipline in a brief time and vanished into the nights.<br /> Bloodline weakness: Silver does aggravated damage and even the touch of silver does lethal damage. Silver can only be soaked with Fortitude.<br /> Disciplines: Celerirty, Fortitude, and the signature discipline based solely on the tribe chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok but a BSD abomination why he must suffer the Harano to became a vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6052-rettile-blitch","name":"Rettile&Blitch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T07:39:16-07:00","id":853466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rettile&amp;amp;Blitch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination?p=853445#post853445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ok but a BSD abomination why he must suffer the Harano to became a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>They develop it after they become a vampire, they become a blasphemy in the eyes of Gaia","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T07:53:46-07:00","id":853470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Origina