 possibly are traveling through the dream realms. Vampires are as equally connected to the Weaver as the Wyrm. The Wyrm does not use vampires they with a few notable exceptions Zettler I'm looking at you are totally unaware of the Garou beliefs. It is a lot easier to change the splats to the game you are using than trying to create a RAW character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok they are connected to the weaver for the human and similar aspect, but they are corrupted wyrm creature, ( if not why the gift track they as Wyrm tainted? )<br /> Ok they don't travel across &quot;spirit realms&quot; ( Uhm the dream and think realm are part of the spirit realm ) but they use a projection to travel inside the plan... and it's wrote in 1 corebook that if a Vampire can reach Umbra and lost inside they become bane of the Wyrm...<br /> I don't want change to the splats... only say, for me, a BSD can be an abomination without falling to harano...<br /> <br /> &quot;Although an astrally projected character remains in<br /> the reflection of the mortal world, she may venture further<br /> into the spirit realms, especially if she becomes<br /> lost.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6052-rettile-blitch","name":"Rettile&Blitch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T08:52:47-07:00","id":853510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination?p=853492#post853492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its advice</div> </div> </div> </div>You bring to much seriously this game man<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is threadcrapping, it's a violation of rule #2\u200b of the forums. Don't do it again unless you want your posting privileges suspended. Darksider</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 03-27-2016, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6052-rettile-blitch","name":"Rettile&Blitch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T10:27:42-07:00","id":853555,"title":"","content":"No they are static the hallmark of the Weaver. Only Vampires that are below a certain Humanity score register to the gift Sense Wyrm, the same it could be argued as any serial killer, rapist, or politician. All of which means squat to the original question. I understand the desire for ONE WORLD OF DARKNESS, but as each splat is written this is not the reality. If anyone thinks this the case great. Then by all means answer the question that was asked how do you make a playable Abomination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T10:49:55-07:00","id":853569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jimflory</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination?p=853417#post853417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to recall something, somewhere about an Abomination giving in and serving the Wyrm having its Gnosis replaced. I wish I could remember...<br /> But, anyway, whether BSD or simply a 'Fallen' Garou, what sort of changes or problems would arise from our little monster changing spiritual allegiances?</div> </div> </div> </div>If an Abomination gives itself over to the Wyrm, the problems with Ego go away, but the issues with Humanity and inability to regain Paths (again, RAW, you can change this) don't. This means that most Wyrm serving Abominations simply plummet in Humanity to 1-2 until they eventually finally drop to 0. This isn't as bad for them as normal vampires, but they're still not the NPC you're looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T11:15:37-07:00","id":853582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination?p=853555#post853555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No they are static the hallmark of the Weaver. Only Vampires that are below a certain Humanity score register to the gift Sense Wyrm, the same it could be argued as any serial killer, rapist, or politician. All of which means squat to the original question. I understand the desire for ONE WORLD OF DARKNESS, but as each splat is written this is not the reality. If anyone thinks this the case great. Then by all means answer the question that was asked how do you make a playable Abomination.</div> </div> </div> </div>ok i see and not only who have an high humanity but also who follow road of the beast... <br /> <br /> Ps. zettler it's not the only vampire... the Giovanni in the pentex, Petaquia and other follow the evil plan of the wyrm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6052-rettile-blitch","name":"Rettile&Blitch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T23:25:58-07:00","id":853918,"title":"","content":"When doing a crossover, don't get hung up on rules as written. If you want this Abomination character to be a certain way, make it a certain way, you don't need to try to fit your concept into the rules. Especially not werewolf rules, since you are running a vampire game. You can pick and choose what ever elements from W:tA that you like and discard the rest to create your vision and a good day role playing experience for your players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T05:12:46-07:00","id":853977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination?p=853918#post853918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When doing a crossover, don't get hung up on rules as written. If you want this Abomination character to be a certain way, make it a certain way, you don't need to try to fit your concept into the rules. Especially not werewolf rules, since you are running a vampire game. You can pick and choose what ever elements from W:tA that you like and discard the rest to create your vision and a good day role playing experience for your players.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems to be the crux of the solution. If I do this, I do it with Vampire 'crunch' and adapt the 'fluff' to suit the story I'm going to tell. <br /> Thank you all!<br /> <br /> Now, the side question inherent in this;<br /> What sort of combination of cultural/tribal/clan origins do you think might best contribute to this Fallen Fuzzy Fellow becoming the villain I'm seeking?<br /> My first thoughts are to go with a Transylvanian Shadow Lord Tzimisce; you'd have the ability to self-rationalize any path to power, a strong tendency to put your own needs above even those of your former Goddess, and a healthy dose of self-loathing for being what he was taught to hate. Sounds like a truly dark individual. Plus, serving the Wyrm with Vicissitude? Just *shudder*<br /> It also brings in the question of whether such a critter might find welcome in service to Kupala (who could easily be seen as a Totem level spirit at least). <br /> <br /> I'd probably take the following off the list immediately. Not because they DON'T work, but they just don't fit the vibe I'm looking for:<br /> Black Furies (though the Greek angle is appealing)<br /> Bone Gnawers<br /> Children of Gaia<br /> Red Talons<br /> <br /> Culturally, really about anything that might have the right mix of tendencies to fight and survive rather than roll over (though just being Garou covers most of that!)<br /> Clan wise, it's pretty open. Odds are we'd end up with a Caitiff anyway.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9106-jimflory","name":"jimflory","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T12:40:39-07:00","id":854154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination?p=853555#post853555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No they are static the hallmark of the Weaver. Only Vampires that are below a certain Humanity score register to the gift Sense Wyrm, the same it could be argued as any serial killer, rapist, or politician. All of which means squat to the original question. I understand the desire for ONE WORLD OF DARKNESS, but as each splat is written this is not the reality. If anyone thinks this the case great. Then by all means answer the question that was asked how do you make a playable Abomination.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree on the One WOD thing. As a many a crossover ST simply get around this by assuming that cosmologies that the different splats believe in Are Wrong.<br /> <br /> It's not hard considering most of the things you hear in WOD are lies/oppinions anyway and all of the different races pretty much try to say they're the ones that created the universe and are therefore better than you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T16:32:33-07:00","id":854242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination?p=854154#post854154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree on the One WOD thing. As a many a crossover ST simply get around this by assuming that cosmologies that the different splats believe in Are Wrong.<br /> <br /> It's not hard considering most of the things you hear in WOD are lies/oppinions anyway and all of the different races pretty much try to say they're the ones that created the universe and are therefore better than you.</div> </div> </div> </div>... no, not really. Certain games actually allow you a peek behind the screen, and once you talk to the Creator, or have God(s) on speed-dial the questions of how the setting works do not end up academical. Werewolf and Mage are worst about this, but Changeling really likes to rain on people's parade too. And that's fine, it's what makes those games unique and their own.<br /> <br /> @Incbill just because you do not register on Sense Wyrm, doesn't mean you're not a servant of the Wyrm by your own existence and predatory depravity that is your life. I'd assume that you're only truly clean if you attain Golconda, and even then you're just an unnatural creep.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9106-jimflory\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9106_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9106\" data-vbnamecard=\"9106\">jimflory</a> I'd skip the Shadow Lords. They and the Tzimisce hate each other truly and utterly, and have been at war for thousands of years.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T17:04:53-07:00","id":854258,"title":"","content":"The Warders of Men (the DA incarnations of the Glasswalkers) are always an option. They're actually a great choice for the social manipulator style character. Unlike most Garou, they highly value the ability to move hidden among humans despite the issues they have with such, as well as influencing human social organizations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T17:18:33-07:00","id":854261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination?p=854258#post854258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Warders of Men (the DA incarnations of the Glasswalkers) are always an option. They're actually a great choice for the social manipulator style character. Unlike most Garou, they highly value the ability to move hidden among humans despite the issues they have with such, as well as influencing human social organizations.</div> </div> </div> </div>That has a lot of appeal, honestly. I do feel like those aspects of a Vampiric existence would come a bit easier to a Warder. Definitely a top choice.<br /> Perhaps Italian? The medieval city-states would make an excellent background.<br /> Then comes the question of Clan. Lasombra leaps to mind for Italy.<br /> Followed immediately by the 'why' of the Embrace. Was it somehow accidental (hard to imagine), or was it knowingly done? Did the Garou seek it out for some ghastly reason? Or was it meant as some unholy punishment or torture? Was he expected to die horribly?<br /> There are lots of great story angles to pursue here.<br /> Any suggestions?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9106-jimflory","name":"jimflory","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T17:31:22-07:00","id":854265,"title":"","content":"Could have been a wrong place wrong time, sire was on the run from the inquisition or a pack of anarchs just grabbed a guy and fanged him to try and buy some time or throw them off the scent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T17:49:37-07:00","id":854270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination?p=854242#post854242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... no, not really. Certain games actually allow you a peek behind the screen, and once you talk to the Creator, or have God(s) on speed-dial the questions of how the setting works do not end up academical. Werewolf and Mage are worst about this, but Changeling really likes to rain on people's parade too. And that's fine, it's what makes those games unique and their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't it also mage that pointed out spirits and &quot;Other&quot; things appear different to people of different beliefs. So meeting the god of love and seeing Aphrodite doesn't really prove anything if the guy next to you sees Venus. Said spirit will even refer to itself as Aphrodite/Venus depending on who's listening, so you can't even be sure if what the spirit is telling the truth or just what you already believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T17:51:43-07:00","id":854273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination?p=854270#post854270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wasn't it also mage that pointed out spirits and &quot;Other&quot; things appear different to people of different beliefs. So meeting the god of love and seeing Aphrodite doesn't really prove anything if the guy next to you sees Venus. Said spirit will even refer to itself as Aphrodite/Venus depending on who's listening, so you can't even be sure if what the spirit is telling the truth or just what you already believe.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is because Mage is Postmodernism: the Game. Not all game lines take the same approach or make the same assumptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 03-29-2016, 04:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T21:39:02-07:00","id":854357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jimflory</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination?p=854261#post854261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That has a lot of appeal, honestly. I do feel like those aspects of a Vampiric existence would come a bit easier to a Warder. Definitely a top choice.<br /> Perhaps Italian? The medieval city-states would make an excellent background.<br /> Then comes the question of Clan. Lasombra leaps to mind for Italy.<br /> Followed immediately by the 'why' of the Embrace. Was it somehow accidental (hard to imagine), or was it knowingly done? Did the Garou seek it out for some ghastly reason? Or was it meant as some unholy punishment or torture? Was he expected to die horribly?<br /> There are lots of great story angles to pursue here.<br /> Any suggestions?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Italy is an interesting choice. Though generally not Lasombra territory at the time since they weren't bothering to fight hard for direct control over the domains that would allow a lot of influence over the Church (which also kept them away from Inquisition).<br /> <br /> Italy would mean the Cappacodians (via the Giovani), and the Toreador as the strongest vampire elements.<br /> <br /> A good option for the &quot;why&quot; could have been to make a sacrificial pawn to throw attention away from a group of vampires (or at another group) expecting the stories of such creatures to result in a ravening beast that would be a nice distraction for more subtle machinations. This would throw the abomination right into the middle of vampire politics when they manage to survive instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T06:08:04-07:00","id":854437,"title":"","content":"Very interesting. A Toreador or Capadocian Warder? Capadocian is probably best avoided...but still worthy of consideration.<br /> As for Italy, isn't Sicily a Lasombra holding in the Dark Ages?<br /> Also the remains of Roman power might well hold leftover (old!) Ventrue, Malkavians, and Nosferatu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9106-jimflory","name":"jimflory","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T10:22:15-07:00","id":854539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jimflory</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/852981-npc-question-bsd-abomination?p=854437#post854437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very interesting. A Toreador or Capadocian Warder? Capadocian is probably best avoided...but still worthy of consideration.<br /> As for Italy, isn't Sicily a Lasombra holding in the Dark Ages?<br /> Also the remains of Roman power might well hold leftover (old!) Ventrue, Malkavians, and Nosferatu.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mediterranean was insane enough since the fall of rome to the17th century that you really don't need to worry too much about actual borders. Just look into interest spheres - half of italy was spanish through times of history, parts of france were germany, parts of italy were france... it took us a loooooong time to actually start getting proper states that we think of nowaday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}